+---
+title: The smallest useful blog
+date: 2026-11-20
+description: An introduction to an ox-powered static website.
+tags: ox, writing
+---
+
+A static blog only needs **source documents**, a transformation, and
+some output files. The rest is policy.
+
+## What we keep
+
+- Markdown as the authoring format.
+- HTML as the publication format.
+- The filesystem as the content database.
+
+This post was rendered by `pandoc`, launched through `Process.run`.
diff --git a/examples/blog/posts/2026-11-23-data-and-effects.md b/examples/blog/posts/2026-11-23-data-and-effects.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e1f7584
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/blog/posts/2026-11-23-data-and-effects.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+title: Data first, effects last
+date: 2026-11-23
+description: How an ox script separates data transformations from Unix effects.
+tags: ox, programming
+---
+
+We model a post as a record:
+
+```sml
+{ title
+, date
+, description
+, tags
+}
+```
+
+The build system transforms that data into HTML. **Only at the edges** does
+it call system utilities to create directories, convert Markdown, and write
+files.
+
+That is the point of ox: *data-oriented first, functional second, imperative
+always available*.
diff --git a/examples/blog/verify.sh b/examples/blog/verify.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..76b8261
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/blog/verify.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+set -eu
+root=$(CDPATH='' cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
+out=$(mktemp -d)
+trap 'rm -rf "$out"' EXIT HUP INT TERM
+ox "$root/build.ox" "$root" "$out"
+python3 - "$out" <<'PY'
+import pathlib, sys, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
+out = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])
+expected = [
+    'index.html', 'archive.html', 'about.html', '404.html', 'style.css',
+    'atom.xml', 'sitemap.xml', 'robots.txt',
+    'posts/2026-11-20-first-post.html',
+    'posts/2026-11-23-data-and-effects.html',
+    'tags/ox.html', 'tags/writing.html', 'tags/programming.html',
+]
+for filename in expected:
+    assert (out / filename).is_file(), f'missing: {filename}'
+index = (out / 'index.html').read_text()
+assert 'Data first, effects last' in index
+assert 'The smallest useful blog' in index
+assert index.index('Data first, effects last') < index.index('The smallest useful blog')
+assert 'Data first, effects last' in (out / 'tags/ox.html').read_text()
+assert 'Data first, effects last' not in (out / 'tags/writing.html').read_text()
+atom = ET.parse(out / 'atom.xml').getroot()
+ns = {'a': 'http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom'}
+assert len(atom.findall('a:entry', ns)) == 2
+sitemap = ET.parse(out / 'sitemap.xml').getroot()
+sm = {'s': 'http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9'}
+assert len(sitemap.findall('s:url', sm)) == 8
+print('blog example: all generated pages and feeds verified')
+PY
